<title>USA: Gerber Scientific Inc Q2 net dips.</title>
<headline>Gerber Scientific Inc Q2 net dips.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH WINDSOR, Conn. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second Quarter Financial Figures for</p>
<p>Three Months Ended Oct. 31, 1996 and 1995</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Sales				     $94,951,000    $90,158,000</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes(1)     6,935,000	7,733,000</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes(1)     (1,800,000)    (2,200,000)</p>
<p> Net earnings				5,135,000	5,533,000</p>
<p> Net earnings per share			  .22		.23</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	   23,327,000     23,912,000</p>
<p>Financial Figures for Six Months Ended</p>
<p>Oct. 31, 1996 and 1995</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> Sales				  $180,759,000     $178,349,000</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes(1)   9,138,000	 14,126,000</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes(1)   (2,400,000)	(4,100,000)</p>
<p> Net earnings			    6,738,000	 10,026,000</p>
<p> Net earnings per share			.29		  .42</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	 23,350,000	 23,954,000 (1)</p>
<p>Included in this year's second quarter and six months ended Oct. 31, 1996 was a gain of $1,032,000 ($.04 per share) resulting from life insurance benefits the company received upon the death of H. Joseph Gerber.  Life insurance benefits are tax-exempt, and as a result the income tax provision rates were comparatively lower in the three- and six-month periods ended Oct. 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
